Interview Questions
Q1. What is the difference between dnf, yum, and rpm?

Answer:

dnf is the newer package manager.
yum is the older package manager.
rpm manages individual RPM files and does not automatically resolve dependencies.
Q2. How do you check your Linux version?
cat /etc/os-release
Q3. How do you check whether Jenkins is listening on port 8080?
ss -tuln | grep 8080
Q4. How do you troubleshoot a server that cannot access GitHub?

A good troubleshooting sequence:

Check IP configuration (ip addr).
Verify the default route (ip route).
Test connectivity (ping github.com if ICMP is allowed).
Test HTTPS (curl -I https://github.com).
Verify DNS resolution and firewall/security group rules if needed.
Q5. Why is dnf preferred over rpm?

Because dnf automatically resolves and installs package dependencies, making installations more reliable and easier to manage.

